# Build-context exclusions.
#
# `docker build` streams the entire context to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs.  With a local daemon that is merely wasteful; against a
# remote context it is a network transfer of everything not excluded here, and
# the two directories below are the largest things in the tree by a wide
# margin -- .pve-matrix/ holds the uncompressed Debian and Proxmox package
# indices (roughly 200 MB) and dist/ holds built artefacts.
#
# packaging/proxmox/Containerfile needs exactly one thing from the context that
# is not source: the shim .deb, passed as SHIM_DEB.  That path is under dist/,
# so dist/ is excluded and the one file is re-included below.  Excluding the
# directory and re-including a file is the only ordering that works: a later
# pattern wins, so the negation has to follow the exclusion.

.git/
.github/
docs/
.pve-matrix/
.act/
.act-logs/
.melange-src/
.melange-build/
.melange-workspace/
melange-cache/
packages/
.deb-verify/
.idea/
.vscode/
.devcontainer/
*.md

# Built artefacts, except the shim package the image installs.
dist/
!dist/pve-container-shim_*_all.deb
# ifupdown2 is built from git.proxmox.com because Proxmox publishes it into
# binary-amd64 only; the Containerfile takes it as IFUPDOWN2_DEB, also a
# context-relative path, so it needs the same re-inclusion.
!dist/ifupdown2_*_all.deb
